@startuml mf-02a-approach
' SRS Section II.1.2.2 — Main Workflow: Delivery, part A (Approach)
' Continues in mf-02b-dropoff-retreat.puml
' Business-level vocabulary only; implementation detail belongs in the SDS.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng mf-02a-approach.puml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam swimlaneWidth 240
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999999

|#F2F2F2|FMS (openTCS)|
start
:The pick-up transport order\nreaches FINISHED;
:Notify WES;
note right: WES re-checks order state on a heartbeat,\nso a lost notification does not stall the task

|#FFFFFF|WES|
:Receive the pick-up completion;
if (Approach already issued?) then (Yes)
  :Ignore the duplicate notification;
  stop
else (No)
endif
if (Assigned vehicle and\ndestination zone both present?) then (No)
  :Task -> FAILED;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Select the approach point:\nthe entry point of the destination zone\nnearest to this vehicle;
if (Any approach point reachable?) then (No)
  :Stay in PICKING_UP;\nthe periodic re-check retries;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Issue the approach transport order;
:Task -> DELIVERING;
note right: The task becomes DELIVERING as soon as the\napproach order is issued, not on arrival

|FMS (openTCS)|
:Route the vehicle to the approach point;

|#FAFAFA|AGV|
:Drive to the approach point;

|FMS (openTCS)|
:The approach transport order\nreaches FINISHED;
:Notify WES;
stop
note right: Continues in part B\n(Drop-off & Retreat)

@enduml
